target/
# Docker ignore patterns without a slash match only the top level, so `target/`
# above does not cover a per-crate target dir.
**/target/
# Bun/npm trees under platforms/ (aivpn-web). These are never needed by the
# Rust images and, for the web image, actively break the build when they
# shadow the freshly installed ones — see platforms/aivpn-web/.dockerignore.
**/node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
releases/
!releases/*.exe
# deploy/docker/Dockerfile.prebuilt COPYs a prebuilt Linux server binary out of
# releases/, which the blanket `releases/` rule above would otherwise hide from
# the build context entirely (COPY would fail with "not found in build
# context"). Re-include exactly the artifacts that Dockerfile references.
!releases/aivpn-server-linux-*
!releases/aivpn-client-linux-*
docs/
# nDPI sources + pcap corpora for the DPI harness — multiple GB, and no image
# builds from them. Keeping them in the context slows every `docker build` by
# the time it takes to tar and ship them to the daemon.
research/
monitoring/
.qoder/
.venv/
*.log
.DS_Store
config/*.json
!config/*.example
